# Accepted-risk list for the image scan (roadmap Issue 216).
#
# `.github/workflows/container-scan.yml` fails on HIGH and CRITICAL
# vulnerabilities in the final image's OS packages, and Trivy reads this file
# automatically when it is at the repository root.
#
# It is deliberately empty.
#
# An entry here is a claim that a vulnerability does not need fixing, so the
# bar for adding one is higher than the bar for the alert it silences: one
# advisory id per line, plus a line above it naming (a) why the vulnerable
# binary or package is not reachable in this image, and (b) what would change
# that. "It is a transitive dependency" is not a reason — neither was anything
# else in the image when it got built.
#
# `ignore-unfixed` is already on in the workflow, which handles the common case
# of an advisory with no released patch. That is the mechanism for waiting on
# upstream; this file is the mechanism for disagreeing with the finding.
#
# Example, for the shape only — do not copy an id from here:
#   # CVE-2026-000000: libfoo's vulnerable code path is the one that parses
#   # .po files; nothing in this image reads one and `apk info` shows libfoo
#   # present only because of busybox-links. Revisit if a base image moves off
#   # Alpine or if the image ever ships gettext.
# CVE-2026-000000
